    "Scouting Notes": "Starter\n Drohan is looking the part in the big league bullpen right now\n Fastball shape is better than the stuff models are giving him credit for in my opinion\n Really like the slider, think that can be a big-time putaway offering for him\n Curveball has a use too, getting more depth and taking more velo off\n Think he's changed the changeup to more of a splitter type of pitch, and it's separated from the sinker shape more\n Don't really think he needs the sinker, but he's a Brewer so he will have it and he will use it\n Cutter is the better secondary fastball in my opinion\n Looks great in the pen, but still think he's a starter long term",
